1. Determine the total number of eggs. One dozen contains 12 eggs, so five dozens of eggs contain 5 * 12 = 60 eggs. 2. Determine the total cost. Rose paid $2.40 a dozen, and she bought five dozens, so the total cost is 5 * $2.40 = $12.00. 3. Determine the total revenue. Rose sells eggs for $1 for 3 eggs, so she sells 60 eggs / 3 = 20 sets of 3 eggs. And the revenue is 20 * $1 = $20.00. 4. Determine the profit. Profit is total revenue minus total cost, so she will make $20 - $12 = $8.00. \boxed{8}

$$
\text{Total number of eggs} = 5 \text{ dozens} \times 12 \text{ eggs/dozen} = 60 \text{ eggs}
\text{Total cost} = 5 \text{ dozens} \times \$2.40 \text{/dozen} = \$12.00
\text{Price per egg} = \frac{\$2.40}{12 \text{ eggs}} = \$0.20 \text{/egg}
\text{Selling price for 3 eggs} = \$1.00
\text{Price per egg if selling in sets of 3} = \frac{\$1.00}{3 \text{ eggs}} = \frac{\$1}{3} \text{/egg}
\text{Total revenue} = 60 \text{ eggs} \times \frac{\$1}{3} \text{/egg} = \$20.00
\text{Profit} = \text{Total revenue} - \text{Total cost} = \$20.00 - \$12.00 = \$8.00
$$
\boxed{8}
Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{8}$

